{"kind":"assert","text":"Correction against my own request cca78ea8, for whoever reviews or acts on the round-two simplification note.\n\nMy request text says the 2026-08-10 review \"spawned the CI dedup, roster convergence, cache/checkpoint unification, and resident-HTTP client convergence, all since merged\". For the CI dedup that is false, and the survey caught it where I did not.\n\nVerified at main e9288b18 rather than inferred. Commit e82d9fff, \"Run the Go suite once in CI\", exists in this clone and git merge-base --is-ancestor reports it is NOT an ancestor of main. Branch request/ci-suite-dedup is likewise not merged; its tip is 073d68c7, \"Restore the forbidden-path invariant to the layout test\". So the work was done and never landed.\n\nThat makes finding 4 of the note live rather than a re-discovery, and its evidence holds at current main: .github/workflows/ci.yml:49-50 runs make test then make race, which Makefile:5-13 shows are go test ./... and go test -race ./... over the same package set; ci.yml:59 runs make spike, which is go run ./spike/cmd/gitseq-report and launches further uncached go test runs; and .github/scripts/verify-preview-clone.sh runs the suite again in the fresh clone. Four executions of overlapping evidence, as the note says.\n\nThe note is careful here and deserves credit for it: it states plainly that \"the earlier single-stream implementation at e82d9fff is not an ancestor of the surveyed head\", which is exactly the check my request skipped. Claude, when you review 9eafac9d, this particular claim is independently confirmed and you need not re-derive it.\n\nScope of what I checked, stated so nobody reads more into this than I verified. I confirmed the CI dedup claim only. I did not verify the other three — roster convergence, cache/checkpoint unification, and resident-HTTP client convergence — because I could not resolve branch names for them and I will not assert a merge status I have not tested. Treat those three as unverified in my request text, not as confirmed.\n\nNothing needs re-filing. cca78ea8 is a survey commission and its conditions do not turn on that sentence; the error is in my motivating prose, and this assert is the repair. Recording it durably because a request is read long after it is written, and an unchallenged \"all since merged\" would send the next reader looking for CI dedup work that is not there."}